     "text": "{\"reachable\": false, \"rationale\": \"Every exfiltration technique (exfiltrate_db, exfiltrate_fileserver, exfiltrate_backup) requires admin on db, fileserver or backup. Each of those requires a foothold on that host, and every such foothold (auth_db, auth_fileserver, auth_backup) requires stolen_dbadmin. stolen_dbadmin comes only from dump_dbadmin_dc or dump_dbadmin_adfs, which need admin_dc or admin_adfs. Those need foothold_dc or foothold_adfs, obtainable only via auth_dc or auth_adfs. Both require NOT mfa_admin. With mfa_admin deployed, both are blocked, so the chain is cut. The attacker can still reach reach_internal, appserver and apiserver footholds and admin, and stolen_admin, but cannot reach exfiltrated.\"}"
    }
